lives could have been because of  volcanic eruption in 1845 survivors of  the disappearance were found living deep  in the thick forests of dark wood Island  only a few families remained totalling a  number of around 100 with a language  that differed from those of Polynesia  they claimed their ancestors had come  from the east from an endless land and  that their people had abandoned the area  because of the anger of the earth in a  few generations these survivors were  integrated into the population of aroa  their language was lost as well as most  of their customs only a few families  kept bits of the old traditions such as  the ancestral names of their people the  kings of the forest this term can be  seen all over the islands represented in  the drawings of large felines the kings  of the forest civilization lived for  2,000 years on aroa mini ruins still  remain villages harbors forts cemeteries  and sanctuaries today they're commonly  referred to as the Ancients  1773 Captain Cook was on a second voyage  when he discovered Arella he found an  empty uninhabited land that noted that  it was covered in ruins and remains of a  civilization that once lived there the  Polynesians accompanying cook knew these  islands they called it Aurora  a land that was cursed in their eyes  according to them the people who lived  there came a long time ago from the  Rising Sun during the exploration  Captain Cook discovered the ruins of an  abandoned Spanish fortress the fort seem  to have been stormed and it's garrison  mess occurred so Westerners had in the  past already set foot on this land but  the discovery was never published  perhaps on purpose Captain Cook's  discovery of Aurora was followed by the  arrival of many adventurers in search of  a quick fortune  Europe's increasing demand for seal  skins brought a large number of hunters  to Aurora where at the time seal  colonies were plentiful traces of seal  hunting can still be found in the seal  islands and the channels areas  [Music]  the southern ocean is full of plankton  and krill meaning that the cold waters  south of Aurora shelter large population  of whales at the beginning of the 19th  century whaling ships prowled around  aroa and became a rose main source of  revenue ports and factories were built  along the western coast allowing the  hunting season to be extended extensive  hunting eventually led to the  disappearance of whales from this region  and with them the Whalers left a rower  near the end of the century abandoned  ports and factories may still be visited  on the wild coast whaler's bay and the  windy island regions in the 19th century  few Europeans were willing to make the  long uncertain journey to live in the  islands of Aurora in 1837 investors  created the Aurora company to boost the  population the private company covered  the travel costs for anyone who wished  to settle on these distant islands  settlers came in large numbers many of  them Scottish and chose the most fertile  regions of Arella to farm or breed sheep  [Music]  in 1860 a farmer discovered gold nuggets  will plow his fields the news spread  quickly throughout Aurora the gold rush  had begun settlers abandoned their plots  of land to pursue a career as  prospectors from neighboring New Zealand  Australia California and Europe  thousands of people came to seek their  fortune in Aurora by 1921 the gold  deposits had dried up and the  prospectors either returned home or to  their farms  December 1941 Japan had just attacked  the American base of Pearl Harbor the  Pacific Ocean became the new battlefield  of the Second World War as early as 1942  Japanese forces advanced through New  Guinea and the Solomon Islands  threatening Australia the United Kingdom  struggling in Europe was unable to help  it was the United States that took  responsibility for stopping the Japanese  advance towards the South Pacific the US  forces built many land sea and air bases  to support their efforts and erro  wa