andoning the native islands  by the end of 1954 the last inhabitants  hiding in the jungle of the dark wood  island were captured and expelled over  the next five years the older World War  two bases were transformed into  state-of-the-art facilities most of the  villages were torn down to make way for  new settlements but there are a few  remnants of the old towns that can still  be found since 1965 the aurora islands  have become a giant US military base a  1953 agreement with the united kingdom  forbid the use or storage of nuclear  weapons on aroa  but they were secretly being kept in  underground shelters the Pentagon relied  on the absence of any civilian or  military surveillance to keep the  weapons a secret however spies managed  to infiltrate the base and information  was made public a crisis broke out  between the u.s. and the United Kingdom  the Aurora nuclear bomb crisis entered  in 1984 after the Pentagon removed the  bombs and promised not to store them  there in the future the departure of the  nuclear weapons was filmed in broad  but some continued to claim that not all  of them at lift aroa with the berlin  walls collapse in 1989 and the  dissolution of the USSR in 1991 the cold  war effectively ended in the absence of  an enemy the American government asked  the Pentagon to reduce its budget  accordingly one of the measures taken  was the closure of several bases  particularly those built outside of the  US so in 1996 the aroer base was  demilitarized and closed with the site's  equipment dismantled and shipped to the  US by the end of 1996 the aurora islands  were once again deserted but not for  long several former soldiers decided to  settle there illegally they would later  be known as the homesteaders though the  Pentagon still held a lease for the area  no one cared about these lost islands in  the South Pacific anymore so they were  put up for auction  and in 2008 JCL purchased surura to  become the hub for the technological  advancement of